<title>INDIA: Indian soybean gains, oil steady, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean gains, oil steady, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices gained 50-100 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on Thursday with traders reporting poor arrivals.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 1,500 tonnes and the market undertone was firm, the traders said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in thin trade. Business was limited as market players awaited the rapeseed crop.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly down on limited export demand. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $294 per tonne for export. Rapeseed extraction was offered at $112 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was quoted at 3,825 rupees per tonne (f.o.r). -----------------------------------------------------------</p>
